        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "General appearance"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Looks tired but comfortable"
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-7",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-7",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Low back pain"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "About 2 weeks, gradual onset, central low lumbar and a bit to the right. Dull ache, can be sharp with bending; up to approximately 6–7/10 if pushed, but mostly described as annoying. Worse after long periods at a desk and lifting shopping. A bit stiff for the first 10–15 minutes in the morning, then eases. Patient thinks it may be related to a new office chair or sleeping awkwardly on the couch."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-8",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-8",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Associated back pain symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Denies leg pain, pins and needles, weakness, bowel or bladder change, saddle numbness, fevers, weight loss, night sweats, or trauma."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-9",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-9",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Lumbar examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Mild tenderness of the right lumbar paraspinal muscles; no midline tenderness. Slightly decreased flexion with pain, but able to move in all directions."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-10",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-10",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Straight leg raise"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Negative on both sides"
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-11",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-11",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Lower limb neurological examination and gait"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Lower limb power, reflexes, and sensation grossly normal; gait okay."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-12",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-12",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Daytime sleepiness"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Longstanding hypersomnolence. Patient says, “I could nap pretty much any time, anywhere.” Reports being unrefreshed on waking."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-13",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-13",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Partner-reported daytime sleepiness"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Per patient, partner reports that she nods off on the couch and at work, and is worried about her daytime sleepiness and driving."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-14",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-14",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Sleep-related history"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Patient reports a history of periodic limb movements on a sleep study about 2 years ago with a private sleep specialist in Sydney; records were not available. Not on treatment. Reports kicking in sleep, disturbing her partner."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-15",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-15",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Sleep-related symptoms denied"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Per partner, no snoring or apnoeas. Patient denies cataplexy, sleep paralysis, and hallucinations."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-16",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-16",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Sleep schedule"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Usually in bed around 10–11 pm and gets up at 6–6:30 am."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-17",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-17",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Drowsiness while driving"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Drives short distances and admits feeling drowsy a lot; has zoned out at red lights but denies actually falling asleep while driving."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-18",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-18",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Mood and concentration symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Reports low motivation, fatigue, poor concentration, and feeling “foggy.” Denies current suicidal ideation."
      }
    },
    {
